  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "Recent agreements between the United Kingdom and the European Union aimed at rebuilding diplomatic and economic ties have sparked political debate. Prime Minister Andy Burnham has engaged in discussions regarding the future of the UK-EU relationship, with reports indicating a year-long process of assessing potential closer ties. While some government figures, including Ed Miliband, have suggested that various options, including rejoining the union, remain on the table, these moves have faced resistance. Former Prime Minister Theresa May publicly criticized the current administration's focus, stating she was dismayed by the prospect of revisiting the Brexit debate. Concurrently, political opponents from the Conservative and Reform parties have raised concerns that the new agreements—particularly regarding food trade—impose EU standards on British farmers who largely do not export to the bloc. The situation remains a central focus of ongoing national political discourse.",
